1
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:13,240
ROY MUSTANG: The Freezing Alchemist?

2
00:00:13,440 --> 00:00:15,060
Really? He's here?

3
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:18,780
BRADLEY: We have information that he managed
to slip into Central a few days ago.

4
00:00:18,980 --> 00:00:20,940
That's why I've summoned you here, Colonel.

5
00:00:21,080 --> 00:00:23,880
I need you and your men to smoke
him out and bring him in.

6
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:25,320
Consider it done, sir.

7
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:26,240
[BRADLEY CHUCKLES]

8
00:00:26,260 --> 00:00:28,720
BRADLEY: I'm glad you're with us in Central
for awhile, Mustang.

9
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:30,900
It's good to know I have
people here I can count on.

10
00:00:30,980 --> 00:00:32,880
- Sir.
- Uh, one last thing...

11
00:00:32,940 --> 00:00:34,960
Our rising young star is here as well.

12
00:00:34,980 --> 00:00:36,920
I'm placing him at your disposal.

13
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:40,620
Forgive me, Fuhrer Bradley,
but just to be clear, are you referring to...

14
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:41,760
I am.

15
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:45,200
I am the Fullmetal Alchemist, Edward Elric.

16
00:00:45,780 --> 00:00:46,860
Ah, damn it.

17
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:49,260
The Colonel's never gonna
let us out of here, is he?

18
00:00:49,540 --> 00:00:52,160
We already bought
our tickets for Liore, too.

19
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:53,760
Does this mean we're not going?

20
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:55,460
I don't know, Al.

21
00:00:55,640 --> 00:00:57,600
For now, let's just get this over with.

22
00:00:57,600 --> 00:00:58,720
- Okay?
- Mmm.

23
00:00:58,860 --> 00:01:00,040
Lead the way, brother.

24
00:01:00,180 --> 00:01:03,660
Kono omoi wo keshite shimau niwa

25
00:01:03,660 --> 00:01:06,000
mada jinsei nagai dsho?

26
00:01:06,980 --> 00:01:12,440
Yarinokoshite'ru koto
yarinaoshite mitai kara

27
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:28,440
Yume no tsuzuki oikakete ita hazu na no ni

28
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:34,780
Magarikunetta
hosoi michi hito ni tsumazuku

29
00:01:34,780 --> 00:01:41,700
Ano koro mitai ni tte modoritai wake ja nai ni
Nakushite kita sora wo sagashite'ru

30
00:01:41,700 --> 00:01:43,320
Wakatte kuremasu you ni

31
00:01:43,320 --> 00:01:48,480
Gisei ni natta you na
kanashii kao wa yamete yo

32
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:51,940
Tsumi no saigo wa namida ja nai yo
Zutto kurushiku seotte'ku n da

33
00:01:51,940 --> 00:01:55,320
Deguchi mienai kanjou meiro ni
dare wo matte'ru no?

34
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:58,900
Shiroi nooto ni tsuzutta you ni
motto sunao ni hakidashitai yo

35
00:01:58,900 --> 00:02:02,040
Nani kar nogaretai n da
genjitsu tte yatsu?

36
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:08,740
Kanaeru tame ni ikite'ru n datte
Sakebitaku naru yo Kikoete imasu ka?

37
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:13,840
Bunai n nante yatte'rarenai kara

38
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:15,720
...kaeru basho mo nai no

39
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:19,020
Yasashisa niwa itsumo kansha shite'ru

40
00:02:19,020 --> 00:02:22,500
Dakara tsuyoku naritai
(I'm on the way)

41
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:26,160
Natsukashiku naru
konna itami mo kangei jan

42
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:33,200
[WHISTLE BLOWING]

43
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:34,240
[FOOTSTEPS]

44
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:36,420
There he goes, that way!

45
00:02:36,420 --> 00:02:38,540
You, halt! Halt or I'll shoot!

46
00:02:40,860 --> 00:02:42,160
[YELLING]

47
00:02:48,140 --> 00:02:49,100
Ah!

48
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:53,560
[BODY THUDS]

49
00:02:53,820 --> 00:02:55,620
Water freezes, water boils.

50
00:02:55,780 --> 00:02:57,440
Either way, you're just as dead.

51
00:03:02,160 --> 00:03:03,220
That's alchemy.

52
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:05,820
ED: What a nasty thing to do.

53
00:03:06,580 --> 00:03:09,920
You of all people should know,
great deeds required great sacrifice.

54
00:03:10,100 --> 00:03:12,340
Isn't that the law equivalent exchange?

55
00:03:12,420 --> 00:03:15,600
Save your breath, the laws of alchemy
don't justify murder!

56
00:03:23,860 --> 00:03:25,540
No transmutation circle!

57
00:03:25,740 --> 00:03:27,400
Don't be too impressed.

58
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:28,640
Now!

59
00:03:38,180 --> 00:03:39,020
What?!

60
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:43,300
No, I had you!
Any water there should've boiled!

61
00:03:43,460 --> 00:03:46,540
If it's any consolation,
you did ruin my coat.

62
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:49,420
An automail arm!

63
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:54,900
A young gifted alchemist...

64
00:03:55,100 --> 00:03:57,760
One who doesn't use transmutation circles...

65
00:03:58,020 --> 00:04:00,380
And who has an auto mail right arm!

66
00:04:00,780 --> 00:04:02,440
I know you.

67
00:04:02,520 --> 00:04:06,960
You are the Fullmetal Alchemist,
Edward Elric!

68
00:04:10,340 --> 00:04:11,780
So...it's not you?

69
00:04:11,780 --> 00:04:13,540
Oh...um, no!

70
00:04:13,640 --> 00:04:15,600
I'm his younger brother, Alphonse.

71
00:04:15,620 --> 00:04:16,960
But he's a runt!

72
00:04:16,960 --> 00:04:18,620
Oh, yeah?! Can runt do this?!

73
00:04:23,440 --> 00:04:26,760
I've heard the stories,
but still I never imagined this.

74
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:29,460
The Fullmetal Alchemist
is just a little kid!

75
00:04:29,780 --> 00:04:31,800
Don't call me little!

76
00:04:32,660 --> 00:04:37,060
You know brother, I don't think he was
really talking about your height just now.

77
00:04:37,420 --> 00:04:39,720
Well even if he wasn't, he still pissed me off!

78
00:04:40,300 --> 00:04:42,760
So you're the one we've been
hearing all the stories about lately!

79
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:44,240
The Fullmetal Alchemist!

80
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:46,420
You're as good as they say,
thanks for the help.

81
00:04:46,660 --> 00:04:48,840
Um, you're welcome, but...

82
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:51,180
I'm really not the one you should be thanking.

83
00:04:51,180 --> 00:04:52,460
There.

84
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:54,480
C'mon, let's get going Al.

85
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:55,660
We got a train to catch.

86
00:04:55,660 --> 00:04:59,240
Oh, okay! Um...
if you think it's alright to leave...

87
00:05:03,400 --> 00:05:04,140
[THUD]

88
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:05,140
[GASPS]

89
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:11,440
What is that?! Steam?

90
00:05:11,440 --> 00:05:13,020
Brother, he's gone!

91
00:05:13,660 --> 00:05:16,040
Damn it, now he really pissed me off!

92
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:20,840
MUSTANG: Looks like you underestimated
your opponent, Fullmetal.

93
00:05:21,080 --> 00:05:23,060
Who is this guy anyway?

94
00:05:23,140 --> 00:05:25,960
You'd know that if you'd listen
to the briefing like I told you to.

95
00:05:26,140 --> 00:05:28,740
But no, you had to go
charging right after him—

96
00:05:28,740 --> 00:05:31,920
Yeah, yeah, I get it, alright?
I'm sorry, 'kay? Whatever.

97
00:05:32,960 --> 00:05:36,040
Next time a superior tells you
to pay attention, you might just try it.

98
00:05:36,820 --> 00:05:37,500
Fine.

99
00:05:37,900 --> 00:05:40,740
Now then, his name is Isaac McDougal.

100
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:44,240
Or he was known back in the day,
Isaac the Freezer.

101
00:05:44,380 --> 00:05:46,240
He's a former State Alchemist.

102
00:05:46,400 --> 00:05:47,340
ED: Former?

103
00:05:47,740 --> 00:05:51,000
That's right.
He served in the Ishvalan war.

104
00:05:51,320 --> 00:05:55,260
During that time, he gave us
no signs that he'd turned traitor.

105
00:05:56,260 --> 00:06:00,260
But after, he immediately resigned
his commission and went into hiding.

106
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:03,720
He's been working with the
anti-establishment movement ever since.

107
00:06:03,840 --> 00:06:07,020
Taking him into custody
is a matter of top priority.

108
00:06:07,460 --> 00:06:09,980
Whether it's dead or alive,
that's up to him.

109
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:12,320
No way, I'm not killing anyone for you.

110
00:06:12,540 --> 00:06:14,100
And that's your choice.

111
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:16,640
Your orders are simply to
help us contain him.

112
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:17,800
That's all.

113
00:06:20,470 --> 00:06:22,440
[CHUCKLES] Off topic...

114
00:06:22,660 --> 00:06:25,740
Have you turned up any leads
for getting your bodies back to normal?

115
00:06:27,140 --> 00:06:29,400
Maybe if you ever gave us time to look!

116
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:31,100
Roy! How goes?

117
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:33,840
Heard you let him put you in
charge of catching the Freezer, huh?

118
00:06:33,840 --> 00:06:35,460
One hell of an nasty assignment.

119
00:06:35,540 --> 00:06:38,540
But hey, could be your chance
to earn that promotion to Central.

120
00:06:38,540 --> 00:06:41,120
Oh, say!
Looks like my timing was perfect!

121
00:06:41,140 --> 00:06:42,880
You two are the Elric brothers, right?

122
00:06:43,040 --> 00:06:43,660
ED: Huh?

123
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:46,840
Wow, it's an honor to finally meet
the youngest State Alchemist ever.

124
00:06:46,860 --> 00:06:48,240
You're a real legend around here!

125
00:06:48,280 --> 00:06:50,300
I'm Lieutenant Colonel Maes Hughes, a pleasure.

126
00:06:50,300 --> 00:06:52,020
Um...you want Edward!

127
00:06:52,020 --> 00:06:54,280
I'm actually his younger brother, Alphonse.

128
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:57,740
What?! You're the Fullmetal Alchemist?
Sorry, I had no idea you would be so...

129
00:06:57,740 --> 00:07:00,360
Go on, say little. I dare you.

130
00:07:00,400 --> 00:07:01,320
MUSTANG: Hughes.

131
00:07:01,320 --> 00:07:02,100
Yeah?

132
00:07:02,140 --> 00:07:04,140
What are you doing here?
Go home.

133
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:07,000
Actually, I'm here on official business.

134
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:10,580
You, Elrics, I understand that
you two don't have a place to stay.

135
00:07:10,860 --> 00:07:12,520
Which means you'll have to come with me.

136
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:13,420
BOTH: Huh?

137
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:16,200
BOTH: Ah!

138
00:07:19,860 --> 00:07:23,300
My wife, Gracia and my daughter, Elicia.
We'd love to have you!

139
00:07:24,660 --> 00:07:26,460
Hi, Princess!
[ELICIA GIGGLING]

140
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:30,280
Ow! Daddy, your beard is itchy!
[LAUGHS]

141
00:07:31,340 --> 00:07:32,160
Like this?

142
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:35,420
Itchy! Itchy!
[BOTH GIGGLING]

143
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:39,540
HUGHES: Look, we have guests!
These are the Elric brothers.

144
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:42,080
Big brother!

145
00:07:42,220 --> 00:07:43,980
Little brother!

146
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:47,700
Nice to meet you. My name is Edward Elric.

147
00:07:47,880 --> 00:07:50,480
This is my younger brother, Alphonse Elric.

148
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:51,620
Get that?

149
00:07:51,640 --> 00:07:53,820
[EMPHASIZING] Young-er broth-er.

150
00:07:53,820 --> 00:07:56,520
But younger means little...
You're little!

151
00:07:57,700 --> 00:07:59,320
AL: Just let it go Ed...
ED: Where do you get off calling me little?!

152
00:07:59,320 --> 00:08:01,600
AL: These people are being nice to let us stay here!
ED: You look in the mirror lately?!

153
00:08:01,620 --> 00:08:04,840
HUGHES: Hope you boys are hungry.
Gracia's cooking his delicious!

154
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:05,900
Huh?!

155
00:08:08,080 --> 00:08:09,180
ED: Ah...!
[ELICIA GIGGLING]

156
00:08:09,180 --> 00:08:10,300
Okay, eat up.

157
00:08:11,280 --> 00:08:12,320
Thanks!

158
00:08:13,880 --> 00:08:16,760
Wow, you weren't kidding!
This is great!

159
00:08:16,880 --> 00:08:19,000
GRACIA: Don't be shy. Eat all you want!

160
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:20,240
ED: Okay!
AL: [GIGGLES]

161
00:08:21,140 --> 00:08:24,560
Alphonse, how you're going to eat
wearing that armor? Take it off, relax!

162
00:08:24,560 --> 00:08:26,440
BOTH: Uh...

163
00:08:26,480 --> 00:08:27,900
Well, you see...uh—

164
00:08:27,900 --> 00:08:30,320
He's not allowed to!
He has to wear it all the time.

165
00:08:30,320 --> 00:08:32,720
It's uh...
It's part of his alchemy training!

166
00:08:32,740 --> 00:08:33,920
[NERVOUS LAUGH]
You know how it is.

167
00:08:33,920 --> 00:08:35,420
I'll eat enough for both of us.

168
00:08:35,420 --> 00:08:37,300
Training, choo-choo!

169
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:41,500
Translation: "Central Prison"
[MAN LAUGHING]

170
00:08:41,520 --> 00:08:45,940
KIMBLEE: Hands down that's got to be the funniest
joke I've heard in a long, long time.

171
00:08:46,260 --> 00:08:49,620
The Freezing Alchemist wants
me to come play his sidekick.

172
00:08:49,820 --> 00:08:51,340
Well as fun as that sounds,

173
00:08:51,520 --> 00:08:54,180
The Crimson Alchemist works alone,
I always have.

174
00:08:54,400 --> 00:09:00,000
Kimblee, if we work together we can bring
down Bradley and his godforsaken military.

175
00:09:00,300 --> 00:09:02,940
You saw the horrors
that took place in Ishval

176
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:04,480
You were there, dammit!

177
00:09:04,580 --> 00:09:06,880
You know the things
Bradley ordered us to do.

178
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:08,640
The kind of man he really is.

179
00:09:08,760 --> 00:09:12,220
That's why you killed all those officers, isn't it?
To send him a message?

180
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:14,120
[CACKLING]

181
00:09:14,140 --> 00:09:16,260
I think you've got me all wrong.

182
00:09:16,480 --> 00:09:20,400
My motives aren't so sophisticated
as revenge or honor any of that.

183
00:09:20,480 --> 00:09:24,140
The reason I killed all of those men
was because I could.

184
00:09:24,520 --> 00:09:25,520
It's that simple.

185
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:28,420
That's too bad, Kimblee.
[FOOTSTEPS LEAVING]

186
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:30,240
That truly is too bad.

187
00:09:31,140 --> 00:09:35,350
[PRISON DOORS OPEN AND CLOSING]

188
00:09:35,900 --> 00:09:37,460
Keep up the good work.

189
00:09:38,860 --> 00:09:40,420
[BODY SMASHES]

190
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:48,740
[DOOR OPENS]
Maes, dear...what's wrong?

191
00:09:48,740 --> 00:09:49,920
Can't sleep?

192
00:09:49,940 --> 00:09:50,920
Guess not.

193
00:09:56,080 --> 00:09:57,660
I know it's in that head of yours.

194
00:09:58,460 --> 00:10:00,280
You're worrying about
those boys, aren't you?

195
00:10:02,160 --> 00:10:04,500
You do know what they call
State Alchemists, right?

196
00:10:04,500 --> 00:10:07,800
The dogs of the military,
not exactly the most popular bunch.

197
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:11,520
I try to imagine what that must be like,
enduring that at his age.

198
00:10:16,040 --> 00:10:17,980
Brother, you awake?

199
00:10:18,340 --> 00:10:19,160
Huh?

200
00:10:19,180 --> 00:10:20,720
Miss Gracia's quiche...

201
00:10:20,720 --> 00:10:22,780
It looked a lot like moms, huh?

202
00:10:22,920 --> 00:10:25,040
Yeah, almost as good too.

203
00:10:25,040 --> 00:10:25,700
Really?!

204
00:10:26,020 --> 00:10:30,460
In that case, I'm definitely adding it to the list
of things I'm gonna eat once I get my body back!

205
00:10:30,920 --> 00:10:31,640
Right.

206
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:33,740
Put it on there, right near the top.

207
00:10:34,020 --> 00:10:34,860
AL: Brother?

208
00:10:35,140 --> 00:10:35,720
ED: Hmm?

209
00:10:36,360 --> 00:10:39,300
AL: I sure would like to get
our old bodies back soon.

210
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:42,020
ED: I know. Me too.

211
00:10:46,640 --> 00:10:47,960
MCDOUGAL: One more.

212
00:10:48,580 --> 00:10:52,880
One more and Fuhrer
Bradley is on his way to hell.

213
00:10:53,740 --> 00:10:55,280
Fullmetal Alchemist

214
00:10:57,080 --> 00:10:58,580
Fullmetal Alchemist

215
00:11:00,300 --> 00:11:04,280
MUSTANG: We have a confirmed report that
McDougal broke into Central Prison last night.

216
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:06,920
Whatever he's up to, he's growing bold.

217
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:08,520
That means our time is short.

218
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:12,860
Close off all roads,
search every square inch of the city.

219
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:15,440
When you find him, shoot on sight.

220
00:11:15,460 --> 00:11:18,050
That is an order from the Fuhrer himself.

221
00:11:19,600 --> 00:11:21,780
But if I find him first...

222
00:11:21,820 --> 00:11:22,660
He's mine.

223
00:11:22,740 --> 00:11:24,320
Get a medic! Hurry!

224
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:26,580
Report to headquarters!
Five men dead!

225
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:27,900
How awful.

226
00:11:27,920 --> 00:11:29,500
It looks like a steam explosion.

227
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:33,460
Raise the temperature of water fast enough
it expands with the force of a bomb blast.

228
00:11:33,620 --> 00:11:36,020
And the human body is 70% water.

229
00:11:36,920 --> 00:11:37,880
Let's hurry.

230
00:11:37,880 --> 00:11:39,840
We have to find him
before he hurts anyone else.

231
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:40,680
Mmm!

232
00:11:43,060 --> 00:11:44,080
Finished.

233
00:11:47,140 --> 00:11:51,640
Impressive reflexes, Isaac,
few are able to dodge my alchemy so easily!

234
00:11:51,660 --> 00:11:52,740
I know that voice.

235
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:54,100
Is that you, Armstrong?

236
00:11:54,640 --> 00:11:55,900
Indeed!

237
00:11:56,180 --> 00:11:57,240
None other.

238
00:12:00,080 --> 00:12:02,840
It is I, the Strong Arm Alchemist,

239
00:12:02,920 --> 00:12:05,820
Alex Louis Armstrong, in the flesh!

240
00:12:05,980 --> 00:12:07,220
Ah, shut it!

241
00:12:09,940 --> 00:12:12,920
I've always wanted to
chop that ego down to size.

242
00:12:14,940 --> 00:12:18,680
Except you'll need far more
than water to quench my fists!

243
00:12:20,340 --> 00:12:21,540
[GASPS]

244
00:12:26,360 --> 00:12:27,440
AL: Major!

245
00:12:32,940 --> 00:12:34,860
The water from his canteen, huh?

246
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:36,780
Thanks for the quick save, Al.

247
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:39,080
Let's go, he's getting away.

248
00:12:39,120 --> 00:12:41,140
Come then, after me, Elric Brothers.

249
00:12:41,180 --> 00:12:42,540
BOTH: Right!

250
00:12:49,800 --> 00:12:52,160
It's been a long time, Freezer.

251
00:12:54,060 --> 00:12:55,760
MCDOUGAL: Well, Roy Mustang.

252
00:12:55,760 --> 00:12:56,500
Heh.

253
00:12:56,740 --> 00:12:59,040
So the Flame Alchemist came out to play.

254
00:12:59,040 --> 00:13:00,840
MUSTANG: You can make this easy on both of us.

255
00:13:00,840 --> 00:13:02,680
I'd rather not fight an old war buddy.

256
00:13:02,700 --> 00:13:05,720
War buddy? Please,
don't flatter yourself.

257
00:13:05,960 --> 00:13:07,660
I knew no friends in Ishval.

258
00:13:07,700 --> 00:13:10,420
Only military bastards,
and their damn dogs!

259
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:21,540
When water meets flame,
the flame goes out.

260
00:13:29,860 --> 00:13:31,400
Dammit, ugh!

261
00:13:34,780 --> 00:13:36,640
Still there! Perfect!

262
00:13:36,780 --> 00:13:38,080
Stop right there!

263
00:13:38,460 --> 00:13:42,040
I was wondering what you were doing
in this alley, so I came back to check it out,

264
00:13:42,060 --> 00:13:43,200
And bingo!

265
00:13:43,440 --> 00:13:45,200
[MCDOUGAL LAUGHS]

266
00:13:46,100 --> 00:13:48,020
There's nowhere to run this time!

267
00:13:48,060 --> 00:13:50,240
Clearly, but who's running?

268
00:13:58,840 --> 00:13:59,980
[GASPS]

269
00:14:01,820 --> 00:14:03,200
An alchemic reaction...

270
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:04,780
On this scale...

271
00:14:05,260 --> 00:14:07,460
Impossible! Unless...

272
00:14:07,640 --> 00:14:08,780
- AL: You don't think he's...?

273
00:14:09,580 --> 00:14:11,500
A Philosopher's Stone!

274
00:14:17,520 --> 00:14:19,720
He's freezing all the moisture in the air.

275
00:14:19,740 --> 00:14:21,340
Edward, Elric.

276
00:14:21,460 --> 00:14:24,520
You've sworn your life to the state
as a dog of the military,

277
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:26,180
But...

278
00:14:26,180 --> 00:14:28,920
Do you really know the ones you serve
or what their true plans are?

279
00:14:28,980 --> 00:14:31,220
Who cares?!
It's not my problem.

280
00:14:31,240 --> 00:14:32,240
Don't be a fool!

281
00:14:32,280 --> 00:14:35,220
He'll lead us to all ruin!
I'm only doing what needs to be done!

282
00:14:35,340 --> 00:14:37,300
I told you, I don't care!

283
00:14:46,060 --> 00:14:47,800
All right! Nice work, Al.

284
00:14:47,820 --> 00:14:49,920
AL: But we still have to stop his alchemy!

285
00:14:49,960 --> 00:14:50,800
ED: I know.

286
00:14:50,800 --> 00:14:52,200
So where is it?

287
00:14:52,280 --> 00:14:54,540
You have a Philosopher's Stone,
don't you?

288
00:14:54,580 --> 00:14:56,180
What are you talking about?

289
00:14:56,260 --> 00:14:58,480
I won't ask again. Where is it?!

290
00:14:58,520 --> 00:15:00,520
And what are you going to do, boy?

291
00:15:00,620 --> 00:15:02,100
You're out of your league!

292
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:12,180
Ahh!

293
00:15:12,180 --> 00:15:15,660
Stand back and prepare for a
display of Armstrong alchemy!

294
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:17,180
He's all yours, Major!

295
00:15:17,360 --> 00:15:23,060
Witness the alchemic art passed
down the Armstrong line for generations!

296
00:15:27,900 --> 00:15:29,100
That's unexpected!

297
00:15:29,100 --> 00:15:31,180
What the heck are you doing?!
You're making it worse!

298
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:32,900
No! I was merely—
[BOOM]

299
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:38,460
AL: The ice walls...

300
00:15:38,480 --> 00:15:39,800
They're merging!

301
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:41,820
But, that would mean...

302
00:15:42,760 --> 00:15:44,600
ED: If they all meet in the middle...

303
00:15:44,740 --> 00:15:47,440
Ah, damn it!
It's Central Command!

304
00:15:47,660 --> 00:15:49,600
BOTH: He's gonna freeze it over!

305
00:15:51,280 --> 00:15:52,060
Major!

306
00:15:52,080 --> 00:15:53,880
Al and I'll try to slow him down.

307
00:15:53,920 --> 00:15:55,960
Can you handle the transmutation circles?

308
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:58,200
Consider them erased. I'm on it.

309
00:16:01,520 --> 00:16:03,100
Fuhrer King Bradley,

310
00:16:03,100 --> 00:16:06,800
For your cold-blooded crimes in Ishval,
I condemn you to a frozen hell.

311
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:08,320
- Not so fast!
- Huh?!

312
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:20,380
Two can play that game!

313
00:16:26,700 --> 00:16:28,680
[ED YELPING]

314
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:30,280
Brother!

315
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:31,440
Too slow!

316
00:16:34,840 --> 00:16:35,860
Alphonse!

317
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:47,540
There's no one in there...
It's empty!

318
00:16:48,960 --> 00:16:53,240
But that...that could only be true
if his soul was bonded to the armor.

319
00:16:54,100 --> 00:16:55,960
So you lost your arm,

320
00:16:55,960 --> 00:16:59,120
and your brother, he lost his entire body?

321
00:16:59,420 --> 00:17:00,300
Heh.

322
00:17:00,480 --> 00:17:02,840
I see. It all makes sense.

323
00:17:04,180 --> 00:17:06,940
You fools committed the ultimate taboo!

324
00:17:07,680 --> 00:17:10,560
You attempted human
transmutation, didn't you?

325
00:17:10,580 --> 00:17:13,480
Alchemy's one and only unforgivable sin!

326
00:17:15,840 --> 00:17:18,540
[SCREAMING] Al!

327
00:17:18,680 --> 00:17:21,680
Dammit! This can't be happening!

328
00:17:22,180 --> 00:17:23,340
No!

329
00:17:23,460 --> 00:17:25,520
He's gone! What I have done?!

330
00:17:27,900 --> 00:17:29,200
[VOICE TREMBLING]
Give him back...

331
00:17:29,240 --> 00:17:30,580
He's my brother!

332
00:17:30,980 --> 00:17:32,460
Just give him back!

333
00:17:32,600 --> 00:17:35,760
He's my little brother.
He's all I have left!

334
00:17:42,260 --> 00:17:43,140
Y'know...

335
00:17:43,440 --> 00:17:46,280
there are some lines you
really shouldn't cross.

336
00:17:46,920 --> 00:17:47,760
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

337
00:18:05,260 --> 00:18:06,280
ED: Give it up!

338
00:18:06,300 --> 00:18:08,280
There's no water for you to use here.

339
00:18:08,280 --> 00:18:10,220
[LAUGHS]
You've forgotten something.

340
00:18:10,260 --> 00:18:13,440
I have all the water I need...
70% of my body!

341
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:14,300
[GASPS]

342
00:18:15,820 --> 00:18:16,880
Ed!

343
00:18:21,120 --> 00:18:22,920
Why can't you fools understand?

344
00:18:22,920 --> 00:18:24,800
I'm trying to save this country!

345
00:18:30,980 --> 00:18:34,500
[CACKLING]

346
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:36,310
Brother...

347
00:18:36,600 --> 00:18:37,440
Brother!

348
00:18:37,540 --> 00:18:39,720
Come on. We're going after him.

349
00:18:39,940 --> 00:18:41,440
I'm not done.

350
00:18:42,840 --> 00:18:43,920
Not even close.

351
00:18:46,900 --> 00:18:48,020
Did we get it?

352
00:18:48,020 --> 00:18:48,980
[GASPS]

353
00:18:50,300 --> 00:18:51,460
Not again!

354
00:18:56,900 --> 00:18:59,920
What do you think of my flames
now, you bastard?!

355
00:19:00,900 --> 00:19:02,320
When will he learn?

356
00:19:02,580 --> 00:19:04,980
It's bad enough that he's useless on rainy days.

357
00:19:11,900 --> 00:19:12,420
Huh?

358
00:19:13,780 --> 00:19:15,060
Bradley.

359
00:19:18,260 --> 00:19:22,620
[CACKLING MADLY]

360
00:19:22,920 --> 00:19:24,060
Perfect!

361
00:19:39,420 --> 00:19:45,620
[CONTINUES CACKLING]

362
00:20:04,600 --> 00:20:05,200
[KIMBLEE CHUCKLES]

363
00:20:07,200 --> 00:20:09,200
Now that is too bad.

364
00:20:09,640 --> 00:20:10,820
Major, go now!

365
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:12,000
Leave it to me!

366
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:15,660
The Armstrong fist will not fail!

367
00:20:31,040 --> 00:20:34,700
[ED PANTING]

368
00:20:36,660 --> 00:20:39,000
ED: Fuhrer Bradley...You're here?

369
00:20:39,140 --> 00:20:41,440
Ah, yes!
Job well done, Fullmetal.

370
00:20:41,460 --> 00:20:43,520
I came out to see if I could lend a hand.

371
00:20:43,940 --> 00:20:45,340
And to think...

372
00:20:45,460 --> 00:20:47,760
that I'd actually
be the one to catch him.

373
00:20:48,400 --> 00:20:51,460
If nothing else, this should
make an exciting story for my son!

374
00:20:53,280 --> 00:20:54,300
[SNEEZE]

375
00:20:54,500 --> 00:20:56,120
HUGHES: Ooh, is that a cold I hear?

376
00:20:56,150 --> 00:20:59,220
Ah, never mind! From what I'm told
you're the man of the hour!

377
00:20:59,340 --> 00:21:02,360
Nah, I just destroyed
the transmutation circles.

378
00:21:02,440 --> 00:21:05,020
The Fuhrer is the one who
actually brought down McDougal.

379
00:21:05,220 --> 00:21:07,700
Sure, but the Fuhrer's
telling everyone it was you!

380
00:21:07,700 --> 00:21:09,200
So congratulations!

381
00:21:09,580 --> 00:21:10,980
Oh, it's like that, huh?

382
00:21:11,060 --> 00:21:13,400
Suit yourself, but some friendly advice...

383
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:18,440
Next time a superior tells you to take credit
for something you didn't do, you might try it for once.

384
00:21:22,660 --> 00:21:23,620
We never did find out whether
or not he had a Philosopher's Stone.
AL: You know...

385
00:21:23,620 --> 00:21:27,000
We never did find out whether
or not he had a Philosopher's Stone.

386
00:21:27,060 --> 00:21:30,160
No, but maybe it'll say
something in the official report.

387
00:21:30,160 --> 00:21:30,800
[KNOCKING AT DOOR]

388
00:21:31,960 --> 00:21:32,480
BOTH: Hmm?

389
00:21:32,480 --> 00:21:34,120
Greetings, Edward Elric.

390
00:21:34,260 --> 00:21:37,080
When I heard you were in the hospital,
I dashed right over!

391
00:21:37,100 --> 00:21:38,860
Ahh!
[BOTH WHIMPERING]

392
00:21:39,140 --> 00:21:42,720
And as I suspected, you're in
desperate need of my assistance.

393
00:21:42,720 --> 00:21:44,720
ARMSTRONG: A-ha!
[ED AND AL YELLING]

394
00:21:45,180 --> 00:21:50,140
ARMSTRONG: You need the example of a perfect
physical specimen to inspire your recovery!

395
00:21:50,180 --> 00:21:52,880
You see? You're looking lively already!

396
00:21:52,880 --> 00:21:54,920
ED: Will you get out!
[ARMSTRONG LAUGHING]

397
00:21:58,020 --> 00:22:00,640
Ah, I see. So Isaac's dead, is he?

398
00:22:00,960 --> 00:22:03,980
That's a shame. I had such
high hopes for him, too.

399
00:22:04,200 --> 00:22:06,440
But...the Philosopher's Stone?

400
00:22:07,400 --> 00:22:08,160
[CHUCKLES]

401
00:22:08,360 --> 00:22:10,060
Sounds like he overused it.

402
00:22:11,400 --> 00:22:14,750
Gluttony, try to chew
quietly, I'm on the phone.

403
00:22:15,960 --> 00:22:18,720
Yes, things are going well here in Liore.

404
00:22:19,500 --> 00:22:20,820
We'll be ready.

405
00:22:21,080 --> 00:22:23,460
It all begins very soon.

406
00:22:28,480 --> 00:22:34,300
Ano hi mita sora akaneiro no sora o

407
00:22:34,380 --> 00:22:39,600
nee kimi wa oboete imasu ka

408
00:22:39,660 --> 00:22:45,360
Yakusoku chigiri shoka
no kaze ga tsutsumu

409
00:22:45,620 --> 00:22:50,500
futari yorisotta

410
00:22:53,580 --> 00:22:58,760
Muri na egao no ura

411
00:22:58,760 --> 00:23:04,140
nobita kage o kakumau

412
00:23:04,180 --> 00:23:13,520
Dakara kizukanu furi saisei o erabu

413
00:23:15,600 --> 00:23:22,740
Table no ue no furuenai shirase machitsuzukete

414
00:23:26,160 --> 00:23:31,580
kuuhaku no yoru o kuru hazu no nai asa mo

415
00:23:31,580 --> 00:23:35,880
zenbu wakatte'tan da

416
00:23:35,960 --> 00:23:41,440
Ano hi mita sora akaneiro no sora o

417
00:23:41,440 --> 00:23:46,640
nee itsuka omoidasu deshou

418
00:23:46,640 --> 00:23:52,080
Hatasenakatta yakusoku o idaite

419
00:23:52,320 --> 00:23:57,140
futari arukidasu

420
00:24:00,720 --> 00:24:03,120
Resembool, a quiet town.

421
00:24:03,360 --> 00:24:08,340
The place where Edward and Alphonse were born.
The home they once shared with their mother.

422
00:24:09,260 --> 00:24:15,820
In the hopes of returning to happier times, the boys commit
the ultimate taboo and are forced to confront the truth.

423
00:24:16,420 --> 00:24:19,580
Next time on Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood

424
00:24:19,580 --> 00:24:22,140
Episode 2: The First Day

425
00:24:23,880 --> 00:24:26,860
The day they resolved their hearts to begin the journey.
